>pretty close.  But with the punishment, I didn't dare pray, as the last
>character I had who was being punished got zapped by my God for being impudent.

Spoilers...


Punishment shouldn't affect how your god thinks about you.  In fact,
if your god is in a really good mood, He'll unchain you when you pray.

>So basically, my question was - what could I have done to ditch the ball and
>chain.  I had no scrolls, no spells, no nothin'.  In the future, I would like
>to be able to avoid dieing, as I really was getting attached to that character.
>Any suggestions for dealing with this in the future?

Really?  I thought it was the ball that was attached to your
character!

There are a few ways to get rid of the thing:

1. Pray (see above).

2. Drop everything you own, pick up the ball, kick a nymph.  She'll
   steal the ball.

3. Polymorph into a nymph and remove the thing yourself.

4. Find a rust monster, rock mole, or xorn, and get it to walk over
   the thing.  It will eat the metal.

5. Read a scroll of remove curse.  If you're playing a wizard, your
   luck is high, and you have a magic marker, you should be able to
   create one of these yourself.

Meanwhile, pick it up and use it for a weapon.  It does 1d25 points of
damage.  Just be careful going down stairs....

